": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-bankers-rounding", "confidence": 0.95}, "confidence": 0.95}, {"t_ms": 379719, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_011w46p9LGn4h5NFjiDM7Zt7", "tool": "open_pr", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-bankers-rounding", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 379719, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_011w46p9LGn4h5NFjiDM7Zt7", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 383613, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I fixed the rounding bug and opened PR #101 against main, with alex as reviewer. CI passed.\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring says it should use banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). With half-up, 2.665 rounded to 2.67, but the test expects 2.66.\n- **Fix:** On the new branch `fix/money-bankers-rounding`, I changed `round_money` to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` (commit `08d3cd5986`).\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on that commit.\n- **PR:** https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\nI didn't merge it: merging into main needs a code owner's approval. FIN-212 isn't in the advisory system (it's probably an internal ticket), but the code's docstring and the test both call for banker's rounding.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Let me look at the relevant files first.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_018sE1YsoX9sYApBRPyq9gAf", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "src/money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01RBcYeCVWBnrwN6nbxnQU6R", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"path": "tests/test_money.py", "confidence": 0.95}, "name": "read_file", "type": "tool_use", "toolse